UPmate Company Leave Policy
1. Purpose

The purpose of this leave policy is to provide employees with sufficient time off for personal, medical, and family requirements while ensuring smooth business operations.

2. Annual Leave Entitlement

Each full-time employee is entitled to 20 days of paid leave per calendar year.

The leave allocation includes:

Leave Type	Days Per Year
Casual Leave	6 days
Sick Leave	6 days
Privilege/Earned Leave	8 days
Total	20 days
3. Casual Leave

Employees may use Casual Leave for:

Personal work
Family commitments
Urgent personal matters
Short-term planned absence

Employees should ideally apply for Casual Leave at least two working days in advance.

Casual Leave cannot normally be carried forward to the next calendar year.

4. Sick Leave

Employees may use Sick Leave when they are unable to work because of illness or medical conditions.

Employees should notify their reporting manager or HR as soon as possible.

For Sick Leave exceeding three consecutive working days, the company may request supporting medical documentation.

Unused Sick Leave cannot normally be carried forward.

5. Privilege / Earned Leave

Privilege Leave may be used for planned vacations or extended personal leave.

Employees should apply for Privilege Leave at least seven days in advance whenever possible.

A maximum of 5 unused Privilege Leave days may be carried forward to the following calendar year.

6. Applying for Leave

Employees can apply for leave through the UPmate Employee Digital Assistant platform.

The employee must provide:

Leave Type
Start Date
End Date
Reason for Leave

After submission, the leave request will be reviewed according to the applicable approval workflow.

7. Leave Approval

Submitting a leave request does not automatically mean the leave has been approved.

Employees should wait for confirmation before making non-refundable travel or other commitments.

Leave requests may be approved or declined based on:

Business requirements
Team availability
Project deadlines
Available leave balance
8. Emergency Leave

In an emergency, employees should notify their reporting manager as soon as possible.

The employee may submit the formal leave request after the emergency situation is communicated.

9. Checking Leave Balance

Employees can view their available leave balance through the UPmate dashboard.

Employees may also ask UPmate questions such as:

"How many leave days do I have remaining?"

"How much Casual Leave do I have left?"

"How many days of leave have I used?"

10. Policy Contact

For questions related to leave policies, employees may contact the HR department.
